      "parameters": {
        "descriptionType": "manual",
        "toolDescription": "Update the inventory record for a book in the Inventory Google Sheet.\n\nUse this tool only after the required calculations have already been completed.\n\nThis tool updates the Stock Quantity for an existing book.\n\nAlways identify the book using Book Name.\n\nBusiness Rules\n\nNew Order\n- Current Stock Quantity = Inventory stock before the order.\n- New Stock Quantity = Current Stock Quantity â Quantity Ordered.\n- Update the inventory with the new Stock Quantity.\n\nCancelled Order\n- Current Stock Quantity = Inventory stock after the order.\n- New Stock Quantity = Current Stock Quantity + Quantity Ordered.\n- Update the inventory with the new Stock Quantity.\n\nQuantity Increased\n- Calculate the difference between the old quantity and the new quantity.\n- Reduce inventory only by the additional quantity ordered.\n\nExample:\nOld Quantity = 2\nNew Quantity = 5\nDifference = 3\n\nNew Stock Quantity = Current Stock Quantity â 3\n\nQuantity Reduced\n- Calculate the difference between the old quantity and the new quantity.\n- Return the unused books to inventory.\n\nExample:\nOld Quantity = 5\nNew Quantity = 2\nDifference = 3\n\nNew Stock Quantity = Current Stock Quantity + 3\n\nRequired Inputs\n\n- Book Name\n- New Stock Quantity\n\nNever update any other inventory fields.\n\nNever invent stock values.\n\nAlways use the current inventory record and the order information to calculate the new Stock Quantity before calling this tool.\n",
